  "body": "Stacked on #3462 (merge #3462 first)\n\n## What changed\n\n3D Finish now accepts protected faces and edge chains.\nThe generator clips cuts outside a keep-out for the flutes, shank and holder.\nThe keep-out covers tip heights from the cut bottom to the clearance plane.\nIt rotates with the work coordinates.\nRapid links rise above protected items.\nThe final full-tool check refuses remaining contact and names the item.\nThe path notes that material beside protected items can remain unfinished.\nWithout protected items, the moves stay the same.\nThe existing command supplies undo and redo.\nMCP help and its committed reference now name the supported kinds.\n\nThe change reuses `AvoidSpec::keepout_region`, `finish_clip::clip_path` and the existing WCS transform.\nThe decision record is `docs/decisions/3347-finish3d-do-not-touch.md`.\n\nReview round 1 (head `f7ff1d080`):\n\n- The branch now contains `upstream/main` `054c1e24b` (a merge commit, no conflict).\n- The Trace fixture of `do_not_touch_click.rs` uses the 1,400 px height of Finish3D. The \"Not taken\" Start point and Exit point groups of #3324 moved \"Pick protected\" below the 1,100 px harness.\n\n## Cause\n\nFinish3D was absent from `do_not_touch_applies`.\nIts generator did not read the protected geometry.\n\n## Tests\n\nApp pins in `do_not_touch_finish3d`:\n\n- `finish3d_accepts_protected_faces_and_edges_and_keeps_unprotected_moves`\n- `finish3d_keeps_flutes_shank_and_holder_clear_of_a_protected_face`\n- `finish3d_refuses_an_impossible_protected_cut_by_name_and_blocks_post`\n- `finish3d_lifts_links_above_a_protected_face_higher_than_clearance`\n- `finish3d_rotated_wcs_keeps_the_protected_face_in_setup_coordinates`\n\nUI pins:\n\n- `finish3d_shows_pick_protected_button`\n- `finish3d_takes_a_protected_face_and_edge_by_viewport_click`\n- `trace_takes_a_protected_face_and_edge_by_viewport_click`\n\nThe first app pin failed on unchanged production code with the unsupported-kind diagnostic.\nAll five app pins and the UI pins pass.\nThe checks include independent tool-band samples and the live protected-geometry check.\nThey cover a named refusal, blocked NC output, undo and redo, and unchanged unprotected moves.\n\nEach mutation failed semantically, then passed after restoration:\n\n- Restore the old upstream allow-list: protected Finish3D picks are refused.\n- Restore the old upstream generator: the holder violates the protected face clearance.\n- Skip the keep-out clipping: the final check refuses the holder contact.\n- Skip the WCS conversion: the rotated path meets the protected face.\n- Skip rapid routing: a link meets the tall protected face with the shank.\n- Remove the named clip error: the refusal omits the protected item.\n- Trace fixture at 1,100 px (the old height) on the merged tree: `trace_takes_a_protected_face_and_edge_by_viewport_click` fails at line 82 (\"the group is armed\"). At 1,400 px, all 8 `do_not_touch` UI tests pass.\n\nResults on the final head `f7ff1d080`:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 171 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (69.5 min). This includes `ui suites: lib` and the eight UI integration suites.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog`: 37 passed, 4 ignored (the 4 are in the heavy lane, which passed).\n- The inherited sccache wrapper stalled each build step (two sccache servers run on this host). All builds ran with `RUSTC_WRAPPER` unset and `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1`.\n\n## Heavy lanes\n\n`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` on head `f7ff1d080`:\n\n- Plan: `app heavy: every target` (`crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs` changed).\n- Result: 208 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (64.6 min). This includes `app heavy: example_catalog`.\n- Two known-fail entries were red as expected: #1950 (`the_users_whole_model_bore_roughs_adaptive_on_each_level`) and #2849 (`fig8_outside_containment_with_em0800_and_clearing_kinds_works`).\n- Logs: `gate-logs/heavy-20261122-222035`.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe Boundary group on the Geometry tab, before (`upstream/main` `6e641dac7`) and after (`f7ff1d080`).\n\n| | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Trace | ![before trace](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/14b2955c7b4c1c7a74aab0681f549db790454316/3495/before-trace-boundary.png) | ![after trace](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/14b2955c7b4c1c7a74aab0681f549db790454316/3495/after-trace-boundary.png) |\n| 3D Finish | ![before finish3d](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/14b2955c7b4c1c7a74aab0681f549db790454316/3495/before-finish3d-boundary.png) | ![after finish3d](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/14b2955c7b4c1c7a74aab0681f549db790454316/3495/after-finish3d-boundary.png) |\n\nBefore: \"Do not touch\" shows only the note that it is supported on 2D Offset and 3D Pocket.\nAfter: \"Do not touch\" shows the Clearance field and \"Pick protected\".\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n`example_catalog` (default and heavy) passed on the final head.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe new protected-item fixtures use the Parallel pattern.\nOther finishing patterns share the clipper and final check but have no new protected-item fixture.\nA physical machine run was not exercised.\nAfter the merge, `upstream/main` moved to `6e641dac7`. The new commits change only process and CI files. `git merge-tree` with `6e641dac7` is clean.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #3462 supplies the shared final guard and is the one-level parent.\n- #3413 changes `do_not_touch_applies`, the unsupported-kind message, and the MCP protection description and reference row.\n- #3426 changes the Finish3D pattern selection in `run_job_arms`. It changes different lines from the protection clip.\n- #3458, #3441, #3439, #3402, #3391, #3387, #3353, #3283, #3251, #3115, #3103, #3059, #3058, #2890 and #2831 change other operation arms or lines in the generator.\n- #3399, #3395, #3378, #3219, #3166 and #3061 change other MCP entries, functions or reference rows.\n\nEach other overlap touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nThe generator also holds different operation arms in one function; their changed lines do not overlap this clip or final guard.\nThe shared allow-list and support text must retain both changes when refreshed.\n\nEffort: max\n\nChangelog: 3D Finish keeps its flutes, shank and holder clear of protected faces and edges and refuses unsafe paths by name.\n\nFixes #3347\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
